Done. Summary:

**Cause:** In `discover/runner.go`, `filterIntegratedGPUs` drops all integrated GPUs by default except those approved by `integratedGPUAllowedByDefault`, which only allowed `device.Library == "CUDA"`. AMD's Radeon 8060S iGPU (gfx1151) was therefore always dropped unless the user explicitly set `OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE`.

**Fix** (`discover/runner.go:412`):
```go
func integratedGPUAllowedByDefault(device ml.DeviceInfo) bool {
	switch {
	case device.Library == "CUDA":
		return true
	// Allowlist of known-good AMD iGPUs (Radeon 8060S family)
	case device.Library == "ROCm" && strings.Contains(device.GFXTarget, "gfx1151"):
		return true
	}
	return false
}
```

**Verification:**
- `go test ./discover/...` → `ok` (including `TestFilterIntegratedGPUs`, which confirms the 8060S/gfx1151 is admitted by default while gfx1103 and generic AMD iGPUs remain dropped, and explicit `OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE=true/false` still work)
- `go test ./ml/... ./server/...` → all pass, no failures
